% issue4_bind_later.glp - POSITIVE (must LOAD clean).
%
% Feature 076 / known-issues Issue 4. A body-atom WRITER occurrence at a declared
% reader (consume, downarrow) position is mode-consistent when its SRSW pair is a
% head-flipped reader - an output hole at a produce (uparrow) head position.
% Authoritative rule: docs/type system/well-typed-clause.md, "Amendment to
% Definition 5.7 clause 2 - Occurrence-Pair Licensing". Acceptance matrix row 3:
% specs/076-typechecker-body-atom-moding/contracts/body-atom-moding-rule.md.
%
% Clause 1 (bind_later/1) is the licensed form: it binds through `=`, whose
% declaration `procedure =(_?, _).` puts arg 1 at a consume position, while the
% head occurrence `Done?` sits at the produce position declared by `_`.
% Clause 2 (bind_later_wa/1) is the historical workaround form - the writer goes
% to a declared produce position - which was accepted before the amendment and
% must remain accepted after it (no over-acceptance, no regression).

procedure bind_later(_).
bind_later(Done?) :- wait(1000) | Done = done.

procedure done(_).
done(done).

procedure bind_later_wa(_).
bind_later_wa(Done?) :- wait(1000) | done(Done).
